     "text": "Schneider and Sons Medical Group\nRe: Latoya Vaughn (DOB 06/18/1980)\n\nJuly O3, 2026: Ms. Latoya Vaughn presented today for her routine follow-up regarding her Type 1 diabetes. Her blood pressure was recorded at 138/71, and she weighed 142 pounds. Ms. Vaughn has been managing her Type 1 diabetes for the past 3.5 years, since her diagnosis at the age of 42. Her A1c level stands at 9.7, and she is on insulin therapy with insulin glargine 100 u/mL and insulin lispro 100 u/mL. She continues to follow her treatment plan diligently.\n\nJanuary 03, 2026: Ms. Vaughn visited for her annual physical examination. Her blood pressure was 132/83, and her weight was 149 pounds. She appears to be in good health overall is managing her diabetes well.\n\nJuly 05, 2025: Ms. Vaughn came in for her scheduled concerning her Type 1 diabetes. Her blood pressure was 140/73, and she weighed 140 pounds. She has been doing well in managing her condition.\n\nJanuary 04, 2025: Ms. Vaughn’s visit today was also regarding her Type 1 diabetes. Her blood pressure was 138/72, and she weighed 134 pounds. She continues to handle her diabetes well.\n\nJuly 07, 2024: Ms. Vaughn presented for a follow-up regarding her Type 1 diabetes. Her blood pressure was 145/77, and she weighed 143 pounds. Ms. Vaughn has been diagnosed with Type 1 diabetes for 3.5 years, with an A1c level of 9.7. She is on insulin therapy with insulin glargine 100 u/mL and insulin lispro 10D u/mL.\n\nJanuary 07, Z024: Ms. Vaughn visited for a medication refill. Her blood pressure was 136/72, and she weighed 133 pounds. She is doing well and continues to manage her diabetes effectively.\n\nA1C trend: Ms. Vaughn’s A1c levels have been as follows: July 2026 at 9.6, January 2026 at 9.5, July 2025 at 9.6, and January 2025 at 9.5. This indicates a stable but above-target level of glycemic control.\n\nSocial History: Ms. Vaughn used to smoke cigarettes at a rate of one per day but quit in June 2025. She consumes alcohol occasionally, averaging about four drinks per week.\n\nGeneral Observations: Throughout her visits, Ms. Vaughn has normal findings in her physical examinations, with no signs of complications related to her diabetes, such as neuropathy, retinopathy, or cardiovascular disease. She remains compliant with her insulin therapy and regular follow-up appointments.\n\nDr. Dillon Humphrey\nEndocrinology\nSchneider and Sons Medical Group\n"
